<title>USA: U.S. nixes changes in lumber pact with Canada.</title>
<headline>U.S. nixes changes in lumber pact with Canada.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States will not make any changes in the U.S./Canada lumber agreement, a spokeswoman for the U.S. Trade Representative's office said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We stand by our agreement and we will make no changes,&quot; said Kirsten Powers in response to a call from the National Association of Home Builders to immediately renegotiate the agreement.</p>
<p>The home builders association said the agreement has caused havoc in the lumber market and has caused lumber prices to rise and the cost of building a typical single-family home in the United States to increase by $2,000.</p>
</text>
